THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

1. Go modules compiled into the released binaries and container images

   None. Everything the agent does uses the Go standard library. A test keeps
   this true: it fails the day go.mod requires a module, so that module is
   named here before it ships. `go version -m /usr/local/bin/lastboard-agent`,
   inside the container, prints the same inventory.

2. Build-time only, not redistributed

   The image at the top of the README is composed by scripts/docs-mockup.ts,
   run with Bun, from screenshots of Lastboard (Apache-2.0, the same project's
   dashboard). Neither ends up in the binary or the image.
